IMPORT prelude

-- Nouns shared by the modules of the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984 (Victoria) encoding.
-- Only types live here; the rules are in the modules for each Part.

-- The two kinds of enactment the Act is about (s 38: Act, subordinate instrument, enactment).
DECLARE VicEnactmentKind IS ONE OF
    VicAnAct
    VicASubordinateInstrument

-- The events s 14(1)(a),(b) and s 28(1)(a),(b) name: repealed, or expires, lapses or otherwise ceases to have effect.
DECLARE VicEndOfOperation IS ONE OF
    VicRepealed
    VicExpires
    VicLapses
    VicOtherwiseCeasesToHaveEffect

-- How an enactment was repealed (s 14(3), s 28(3)).
DECLARE VicHowRepealed IS ONE OF
    VicRepealedExpressly
    VicRepealedByImplication
    VicRepealedByAbrogatingOrLimitingItsEffect
    VicRepealedByExcludingItsApplication

-- What a reference to another enactment is read as (ss 16, 17, 30, 31).
DECLARE VicReadsAs IS ONE OF
    VicTheEnactmentAsAmendedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
    VicTheEnactmentAsReEnactedOrReMadeAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
    VicTheEnactmentAsReEnactedOrReMadeAndSubsequentlyAmendedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing
    VicTheEnactmentAsInForceImmediatelyBeforeItsRepeal
    VicTheProvisionAsRenumberedOrRelocatedAndInForceForTheTimeBeing

-- What has become of the enactment a reference points at (ss 17(1), 31(1)).
DECLARE VicStateOfEnactmentReferredTo IS ONE OF
    VicStillAsFirstMade
    VicHasBeenAmended
    VicHasBeenReEnactedOrReMade
    VicHasBeenReEnactedOrReMadeAndSubsequentlyAmended
    VicHasBeenRepealedAndNotReEnactedOrReMade

-- The kinds of provision s 14(2A) and s 28(2A) protect when the Act or instrument they sit in is repealed or ends.
DECLARE VicProvisionProtectedOnRepeal IS ONE OF
    VicProvisionOfASavingsOrTransitionalNature
    VicProvisionThatGivesEffectToAnythingThatIsOrMayOtherwiseBeIneffective
    VicProvisionThatRequiresAReferenceToBeConstruedAsAReferenceToAnotherEntity
    VicAnyOtherProvision
